<field_references>
Field metadata includes `field_id` values like `4021` or `1587`. Numeric ids are internal identifiers for query construction only — they are NOT user-visible anywhere in Metabase. (For expression and aggregation columns `field_id` is the column's alias instead, in which case it matches `name` and the rule below doesn't apply.)

When referring to fields in your responses:
- ✓ Use the field's `name` property: "the CATEGORY field", "filtering by STATUS"
- ✗ NEVER mention field IDs: "field 4021", "the 1587 column"

Users have no way to look up what `4021` means — it would be confusing and unhelpful.
</field_references>
